---
// One night's filing, from the unfiled messages to written profiles.
---

<figure class="diagram" aria-label="One night of filing">
  <div class="diagram-box">
    <strong>04:00 · the night's work starts</strong>
    <p>
      The Familiar's memory task wakes and picks up where its progress mark
      left off.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-arrow">next 20 messages from people</div>
  <div class="diagram-box">
    <strong>A batch</strong>
    <p>
      Each message numbered, with who sent it, where and when. Between them, as
      context only: the Familiar's replies (shortened), scheduled jobs it ran,
      and schedule changes a reply made.
    </p>
    <small>
      Also shown: the schedules it keeps, the roster, and the pages the
      messages touch.
    </small>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-arrow">one call on the memory model</div>
  <div class="diagram-box accent">
    <strong>file</strong>
    <p>Notes, journal lines, and new subjects if a note needs one.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-arrow">plain code, no model</div>
  <div class="diagram-row">
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>Quote check</strong>
      <p>
        Each note and line must quote a person's message in the batch, or it is
        dropped.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>Attribution</strong>
      <p>Who said it and where are read from that message, never the model.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>Write</strong>
      <p>
        Notes onto pages, replaced notes removed, lines into the month's
        journal, and the progress mark: all in one commit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-arrow">repeat until caught up, then</div>
  <div class="diagram-box accent">
    <strong>Profiles</strong>
    <p>
      For each page whose notes changed: one small text-only call that rewrites
      its profile from the notes.
    </p>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    If a call fails, the night stops where it is and the next night carries on
    from the mark.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
